00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:13,500
The Real Charlie Chaplin is a documentary, drama film directed by James Spinney.

2
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:21,000
A look at the life and work of Charlie Chaplin in his own words featuring
an in-depth interview he gave to Life magazine in 1966.

3
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:28,500
Self - Narrator (voice), played by Pearl Mackie.

4
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Self (archive footage), played by Charlie Chaplin.

5
00:35:37,500 --> 00:35:43,500
Charlie Chaplin 1966, played by Jeff Rawle.

6
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Richard Meryman, played by Matthew Wolf.

7
00:49:52,500 --> 00:49:58,500
Roddy McDowall, played by Dickie Beau.

8
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Effie Wisdom, played by Anne Rosenfeld.

9
01:04:07,500 --> 01:04:13,500
Charlie Chaplin is a 2002 Indian Tamil-language comedy film directed by Sakthi
Chidambaram, starring Prabhu and Prabhu Deva in the lead roles.

10
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
Abhirami, Gayathri Raguram and Livingston play other supporting roles.

11
01:18:22,500 --> 01:18:28,500
It was released on 15 February 2002, and became a commercial success.

12
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
Prabhu won the Tamil Nadu State Film Award Special
Prize for his performance in the film.

13
01:32:37,500 --> 01:32:43,500
The film's commercial success led to remakes in several languages, such as in Telugu as Pellam Oorelithe, Hindi as No Entry, Malayalam
as Happy Husbands, Kannada as Kalla Malla Sulla, Marathi as No Entry Pudhe Dhoka Aahey and in Bengali as Kelor Kirti.

14
01:39:45,000 --> 01:39:51,000
The film explores themes of comedian, biography, actor.

15
01:46:52,500 --> 01:46:58,500
The tone is emotional.
